Original LLVM declaration-profile audit, 2026-09-16.
Authority: reviewed R01/F01 in output/compiler-review/20260909/decisions.md.
Source pin: llvm-test-suite 2919e55176a572ee085cb46b291c47b7092c363e.
Fixed image: evo-flight-lab:sealed, linux/arm64, network none.
GCC-14 14.2.0-19 and Clang-19 19.1.7.

The original 20260915T152557Z compilation database and 655 historical
E1001/E2001 programs were inspected. Each probe keeps the source and semantic
options, supplies the profile's default -std=gnu11 when no mode was specified,
and removes diagnostic options (-w/-W*) to expose the language boundary.
This is not the original benchmark invocation: its suppressed diagnostics
allowed the reference build to proceed. No reference PASS becomes an oracle
failure, and no original source is rewritten with prototypes or new types.

636 programs are refused by both fixed compilers for an implicit declaration
or implicit type in this mode. They divide into:
6 file-scope implicit int; 314 implicit return type; 6 implicit parameter type;
292 implicit library call; 2 implicit ordinary call; 16 where GCC first names
the implicit return type and Clang first names an implicit parameter type.
The other 19 programs remain outside this disposition table.

Full measured probe argv, removed diagnostic flags, source SHA-256 and both
first diagnostics: .build/vector-targeted/llvm-profile-declarations2.jsonl.
Each applicable ledger row retains the source hash, original full compilation
argv and both first diagnostics. Source or command changes invalidate that
disposition; in particular GNU89 or -fwrapv cannot inherit a GNU11 finding.
The status is not-applicable under the explicit reviewed profile, not PASS,
not FP-deferred, and not a claim that either original reference run failed.
Raw subject outcomes and all program identities remain unchanged.
